    <item>
      <title>Automation in Enterprise Systems</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/devika-portfolio/writing/systems-operations/automation-in-enterprise-systems/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 12 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <author>gdevika423@gmail.com (Devika Jallegowda)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/devika-portfolio/writing/systems-operations/automation-in-enterprise-systems/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;h2&gt;Context&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;context&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#context&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Enterprise systems often involve large operational workloads performed by engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Observation&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;observation&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#observation&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Many operational tasks such as monitoring, log analysis, and incident detection follow predictable workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Example&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;example&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#example&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Automation systems can monitor signals across infrastructure environments and alert engineers when intervention is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This reduces manual monitoring effort and improves operational visibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Takeaway&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;takeaway&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#takeaway&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Automation becomes valuable when it reduces repetitive operational tasks while improving system reliability.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Operations as Products</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/devika-portfolio/writing/systems-operations/operations-as-products/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 12 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <author>gdevika423@gmail.com (Devika Jallegowda)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/devika-portfolio/writing/systems-operations/operations-as-products/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;h2&gt;Context&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;context&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#context&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Operations teams often manage complex systems through manual workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Observation&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;observation&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#observation&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Many operational tasks follow predictable patterns that make them strong candidates for automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Example&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;example&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#example&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Monitoring systems, incident management workflows, and infrastructure maintenance processes can often be converted into structured software platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Takeaway&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;takeaway&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#takeaway&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Viewing operations through a product lens can reveal opportunities to design scalable systems rather than relying on manual workflows.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
